==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
You'll be able to get about 2 levels into your Worker Cat before you save up enough to stall the Dread Bore out. He moves really fast, attacks really fast and revives after only 5 seconds.

Tanky Zombie Killer Ubers like [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S Lionheart]] or [[AAA Wunder (Uber Rare Cat)|NNN Wunder]] are your best bet here as they hit the Zombies and Reds equally hard. Still, pretty much any Zombie Killer will help you. When the Shy Boys spawn, you will need those anti-Reds out on the field already so be prepared. Zackie Peng joins the Shy Boys and your meatshields are put to the test.

Once the Dread Bore and initial Shy Boy are dead, another Shy Boy will spawn and then you'll deal with The Face. He isn't going to really hurt your cats too bad because he attacks so slow, but he is rather tanky and may take you a while to defeat.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Same deal here but everything is buffed. You also have Thrillerz with the double-burrow to deal with so more Zombie Killer units the better.

The match plays out the same this time with Dread Bore being the 2nd threat to spawn but the first threat to be dealt with. Sending out early Crazed cats to make him burrow ASAP is imperative. If you can lock down Dread Bore with Freeze, Slow, or Weaken, then you can save up for anti-Red/Floating Ubers to deal with the Shy Boys (and later, the Face). Then you can try to finish the Bore and Shy Boys off at about the same pace. The Face is just there to be intimidating as the Dread Bore is the real boss of the stage.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The most notable change here is that I.M. Phace joins the team; other than that, nothing much changes. Use the same strategy from previous outbreaks and incorporate anti-Alien/Floating units like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psycho Cat]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] for I.M. Phace.

